 "lines": {
  "status": 200,
  "body": {
   "blocks": [
    [
     {
      "text": "PostgreSQL",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "Documentation \u2192 PostgreSQL 18",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "Supported Versions: Current (18) / 17 / 16 / 15 / 14",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "Development Versions: 19 / devel",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "Unsupported versions: 13 / 12 / 11 / 10 / 9.6 / 9.5 / 9.4 / 9.3 / 9.2 / 9.1 / 9.0 / 8.4 / 8.3 / 8.2 / 8.1 / 8.0 /",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "7.4 / 7.3 / 7.2",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "Search the documentatio",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "2.5. Querying a Table",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "Prev Up Chapter 2. The SQL Language Home Next",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "To retrieve data from a table, the table is queried. An SQL SELECT statement is used to do this. The",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "statement is divided into a select list (the part that lists the columns to be returned), a table list (the part",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "that lists the tables from which to retrieve the data), and an optional qualification (the part that specifies",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "any restrictions). For example, to retrieve all the rows of table weather, type:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "SELECT * FROM weather;",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "Here * is a shorthand for \u201call columns\u201d. [2] So the same result would be had with:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "SELECT city, temp_lo, temp_hi, prcp, date FROM weather;",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "The output should be:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "     city      | temp_lo | temp_hi | prcp |    date",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "---------------+---------+---------+------+------------",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " San Francisco |      46 |      50 | 0.25 | 1994-11-27",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " San Francisco |      43 |      57 |    0 | 1994-11-29",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " Hayward       |      37 |      54 |      | 1994-11-29",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "(3 rows)",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "You can write expressions, not just simple column references, in the select list. For example, you can",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "do:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "SELECT city, (temp_hi+temp_lo)/2 AS temp_avg, date FROM weather;",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "This should give:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "     city      | temp_avg |    date",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "---------------+----------+------------",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " San Francisco |       48 | 1994-11-27",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " San Francisco |       50 | 1994-11-29",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " Hayward       |       45 | 1994-11-29",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "(3 rows)",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "Notice how the AS clause is used to relabel the output column. (The AS clause is optional.)",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "A query can be \u201cqualified\u201d by adding a WHERE clause that specifies which rows are wanted. The WHERE",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "clause contains a Boolean (truth value) expression, and only rows for which the Boolean expression is",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "true are returned. The usual Boolean operators (AND, OR, and NOT) are allowed in the qualification. For",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "example, the following retrieves the weather of San Francisco on rainy days:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "SELECT * FROM weather",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "    WHERE city = 'San Francisco' AND prcp \u003e 0.0;",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "Result:",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "     city      | temp_lo | temp_hi | prcp |    date",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "---------------+---------+---------+------+------------",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "     city      | temp_lo | temp_hi | prcp |    date",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "---------------+---------+---------+------+------------",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " San Francisco |      46 |      50 | 0.25 | 1994-11-27",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "(1 row)",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "You can request that the results of a query be returned in sorted order:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "SELECT * FROM weather",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "    ORDER BY city;",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "     city      | temp_lo | temp_hi | prcp |    date",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "---------------+---------+---------+------+------------",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " Hayward       |      37 |      54 |      | 1994-11-29",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " San Francisco |      43 |      57 |    0 | 1994-11-29",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " San Francisco |      46 |      50 | 0.25 | 1994-11-27",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "In this example, the sort order isn't fully specified, and so you might get the San Francisco rows in",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "either order. But you'd always get the results shown above if you do:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "SELECT * FROM weather",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "    ORDER BY city, temp_lo;",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "You can request that duplicate rows be removed from the result of a query:",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "SELECT DISTINCT city",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "    FROM weather;",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "     city",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "---------------",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " Hayward",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": " San Francisco",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "(2 rows)",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "Here again, the result row ordering might vary. You can ensure consistent results by using DISTINCT",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "and ORDER BY together: [3]",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "SELECT DISTINCT city",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "    FROM weather",
      "mono": true
     },
     {
      "text": "    ORDER BY city;",
      "mono": true
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "[3] In some database systems, including older versions of PostgreSQL, the implementation of DISTINCT",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "automatically orders the rows and so ORDER BY is unnecessary. But this is not required by the SQL",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "standard, and current PostgreSQL does not guarantee that DISTINCT causes the rows to be ordered.",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "If you see anything in the documentation that is not correct, does not match your experience with the",
      "mono": false
     },
     {
      "text": "particular feature or requires further clarification, please use this form to report a documentation issue.",
      "mono": false
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "text": "Site footer",
      "mono": false
     }
    ]
   ]
  }
 }
}
